{
  "architecturalBrief": {
    "planningIntent": "To design a climate-adaptive, constraint-driven 3BHK residential house in the Kerala Traditional style for a family of four, adhering to a moderate budget and maximizing spatial efficiency on a compact East-facing plot.",
    "siteResponse": "The East-facing plot in Kochi dictates a design that embraces morning sun while mitigating harsh afternoon heat. Deep verandahs, strategic window placements, and an internal lightwell/courtyard are employed to ensure comfort and natural ventilation. Parking is positioned at the front-left, providing direct access to the main entrance.",
    "orientationStrategy": "Main public areas (Living, Verandah) are oriented towards the East for morning light and street connection. Master Bedroom is positioned on the cooler South-West. Windows are strategically placed to maximize cross-ventilation across the living-dining axis, with shaded openings on less favorable orientations.",
    "publicPrivateStrategy": "Ground Floor hosts the public (Living, Dining), semi-private (Courtyard), and service zones (Kitchen, Utility), along with an accessible Master Suite for convenience. The First Floor is dedicated to private spaces, including two secondary bedrooms and a small study/family lounge.",
    "serviceStrategy": "Kitchen and Utility are consolidated at the rear-left of the ground floor, adjacent to the dining area, creating a compact and efficient wet zone. The ground floor master bath is directly adjacent to the master bedroom, minimizing plumbing runs. The first-floor common bath is stacked above the kitchen/utility area for vertical plumbing efficiency.",
    "circulationStrategy": "A clear, linear circulation spine is established from the East-facing entrance, connecting the public living spaces to the dining, kitchen, and the ground floor master bedroom. A dog-legged staircase serves as the primary vertical circulation, centrally located for easy access to all ground and first-floor areas.",
    "climateStrategy": "Inspired by Kerala's hot-humid climate, the design incorporates a deep front verandah and a first-floor balcony for shading. An internal courtyard/lightwell introduces natural light and promotes stack effect ventilation. Pitched roofs and strategically placed fenestration facilitate cross-ventilation and heat dissipation, reducing reliance on mechanical cooling.",
    "accessibilityStrategy": "A ground-floor master bedroom ensures accessibility for family members. The design prioritizes clear pathways and adequate room dimensions for comfortable movement within the primary living zones.",
    "styleStrategy": "The design strongly embraces the Kerala Traditional architectural style, featuring deep shaded verandahs, pitched roofs, natural material palettes (wood, terracotta tones), and an emphasis on internal courtyards for light and ventilation. The overall massing is kept humble yet elegant, reflecting regional aesthetics."
  },
